 t←cid MySQLQuery q;sql;binds;c;d;f;desc;names;data;i;Check;Utf8
⍝ Run a SELECT and return a namespace with one vector per column.
⍝ Also sets t.columns (the names) and t.data (the result as a matrix).
⍝
⍝   s←db MySQLQuery 'SELECT region, qty*price AS amount FROM sales'
⍝   s.region  s.amount  s.columns  s.data
⍝
⍝ With parameters, use SQAPL bind markers :n<type: and pass the values:
⍝   s←db MySQLQuery 'SELECT * FROM sales WHERE region=:1<C20: AND qty>:2<I:' 'North' 5
⍝   types: I integer, F float, C<n> text up to n characters
⍝
⍝ Column names must be valid APL names, so alias expressions (AS amount).
⍝ NULLs come back as 0 (numbers) or '' (text). Dates come back as text
⍝ ('2026-03-14'). BIGINTs are converted from text to numbers.

 (sql binds)←{1≥|≡⍵:⍵ ⍬ ⋄ (⊃⍵)(1↓⍵)}q
 c←2⊃#.SQA.CursorName cid
 Check←{0=⊃⍵:⍵ ⋄ _←#.SQA.Close c ⋄ ⎕SIGNAL⊂('EN' 11)('Message'('MySQLQuery: ',⍕3⊃⍵))}
 {}Check #.SQA.Prepare c sql
 {}Check #.SQA.Exec(⊂c),binds
 d←Check 0 #.SQA.Describe c
 f←Check 1 #.SQA.Fetch c
 {}#.SQA.Close c

 ⍝ Describe lists bind parameters first, then the result columns
 desc←(≢binds)↓2⊃2⊃d
 names←⊃∘⊃¨desc
 data←⊃2⊃f
 :If 0∊⍴data ⋄ data←(0,≢names)⍴0 ⋄ :EndIf

 ⍝ SQAPL returns text as UTF-8 bytes; decode it (leave numbers alone)
 Utf8←{0::⍵ ⋄ (0=≢⍵)∨' '≠⊃0⍴⍵:⍵ ⋄ 'UTF-8'⎕UCS ⎕UCS ⍵}
 data←Utf8¨data

 ⍝ BIGINT columns (ODBC type ¯5, e.g. COUNT(*)) arrive as text; make numbers
 :For i :In ⍸¯5=(5⊃⊃)¨desc         ⍝ 5th item of a column's description = SQL type
     data[;i]←{0=≢⍵:0 ⋄ ⊃2⊃⎕VFI ⍵}¨data[;i]
 :EndFor

 :If ¯1∊⎕NC↑names
     ⎕SIGNAL⊂('EN' 11)('Message'('MySQLQuery: alias columns to valid APL names: ',⍕names))
 :EndIf
 t←⎕NS ⍬
 t.columns←names
 t.data←data
 :For i :In ⍳≢names
     t.⍙v←data[;i]
     t⍎(i⊃names),'←⍙v'
 :EndFor
 t.⎕EX'⍙v'
